ge \\\\\\\"Please include an '@' in the email address.\\\\\\\" No success toast shown in either case.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-10\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Invalid job data accepted (min salary > max salary, no required skill)\", \"actual\": \"Posted a job titled 'QA Test Engineer' with Minimum Salary=150000 and Maximum Salary=100000 (min > max) and with zero required skills added. The form accepted it and showed 'Job posted successfully! Your job listing is now live and visible to job seekers.' The new listing appears in the dashboard as 'Austin, TX · $150k - $100k · Posted Yesterday' with no skill tags, instead of being rejected with validation feedback.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-11\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Duplicate email application accepted\", \"actual\": \"Submitted a second application to job-1 using the same email (alice.johnson@example.com) already used for that job. App showed success toast 'Application submitted!' and the employer dashboard's Applications(4) list for Senior Frontend Developer now shows two separate entries ('Alice Johnson' and 'Alice Johnson Duplicate') both with email alice.johnson@example.com, instead of rejecting the duplicate or leaving the original unchanged.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-13\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Submitting Alice Johnson's application produced a visible toast confirmation and the entry appears exactly once (as 'Alice Johnson') under Senior Frontend Developer's application list in the employer dashboard, with the submitted name/email/phone/message.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-14\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Each filter change immediately updated the result count and list without needing a page reload (10 -> 3 -> 1 -> 0). No-results state showed 'No jobs found / Try adjusting your filters or search terms'. Clear filters button restored full list of 10 jobs.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-19\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Data does not persist across page reload\", \"actual\": \"Before reload: 9 jobs existed (8 original + 1 new 'Backend Software Engineer'; 'QA Test Engineer' had been deleted), and Senior Frontend Developer had 4 applications (2 submitted during this test session). After navigating to http://localhost:6003/ (reload), the homepage reverted to 'Showing 8 jobs' (original seed set only, new job gone), and the employer dashboard reverted to Active Jobs=5, Total Applications=3 (back to the original seed applications, both test-submitted applications and the new job/deletion were lost). Published jobs, submitted applications, and job deletions do not persist after reload.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-15\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Each job card (e.g. Senior Frontend Developer, Registered Nurse, Data Analyst) displays industry badge, employment type badge, title, company, location, salary range, posting date, and required skill tags.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-16\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"job-1 details page shows title, company (TechCorp Solutions), industry (Technology), employment type (Full-time), location (San Francisco, CA), salary ($140k-$180k), posting date (Posted Jan 15), full description with responsibilities/requirements, and required skills (React, TypeScript, CSS, Node.js) - matches the listing card.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-17\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Each application entry in the dashboard shows applicant name, email, phone when provided (e.g. Alex Johnson 555-0101), message, and a submission date (e.g. Jan 20, Jan 22, Yesterday) as separate distinct cards.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-20\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Newly created job/application dates show as 'Yesterday' instead of 'Today'\", \"actual\": \"Browser clock confirmed as Tue Aug 25 20